WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:00.600
We are

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.201
covering the

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:01.935
Trump indictment

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.303
from the nation's capital

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.437
to the campaign trail.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.505
CNN correspondent

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.940
Jack Cohen is in Washington

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.441
with details on the charges

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.542
in the indictment.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.044
Randi, Kaye is in Miami

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.779
with a look at security

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.781
precautions for Trump's court appearance.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:15.782
And Elaina, TREENE

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.250
is covering the campaign.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.184
Trump holds rallies

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.520
today in Georgia and North Carolina.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:21.488
We'll start

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.189
first with CNN national security

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.591
and justice reporter

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:26.993
Zach Cohen in Washington

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.228
to break down the nuts

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.163
and bolts of the indictment.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:30.663
Yeah.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:30.997
Zach,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:31.898
there are a lot of details

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.033
in those documents.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.167
Stunning details.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.002
Tell us what you're learning.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:37.504
Yeah, Victor.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:38.505
And prosecutors

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.173
are alleging that Donald Trump

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.475
knowingly, intentionally

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.543
retained hundreds

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.677
of classified documents.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:45.845
If you look at the charges,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.013
the 37 counts

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.681
in this indictment document.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.682
31 of them

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.550
have to do

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.785
with the willful retention

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.820
of national defense information.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.654
Now, that is

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.156
pretty much exactly what it sounds like.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.357
And if you look at this one

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.258
paragraph, paragraph

00:00:58.258 --> 00:00:59.893
three of the indictment, it spells it out

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:00.860
very clearly.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.861
The kind of information

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.462
we're talking about.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.496
We're talking about information

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:06.699
related to US weapons systems, US defense

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:07.801
programs, US

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.869
nuclear capabilities, Really,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.171
this is these documents

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.439
did deal with some of our nation's

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.973
most sensitive secrets.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.241
And it also

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.676
it came from a variety of different

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.078
agencies, intelligence agencies

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.113
that included the CIA,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.414
that included the NSA.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.916
So a large variety

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.384
of very sensitive documents

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.152
were found at Mar a Lago.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:26.519
And Jack

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.420
Smith really underscored

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.721
the seriousness of that

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.123
in his remarks yesterday.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.057
Now, the other counts

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:31.891
that we're looking at here

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.494
deal with obstruction and concealment.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.463
There's even a reference there to

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.397
something Trump allegedly

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.699
said to his lawyers before

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.202
the FBI came down to search Mar a Lago.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.670
He said something to the effect of,

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.604
wouldn't it be better

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.538
if we just told them

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.240
we didn't have anything here?

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.608
And of course, he knew full

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.877
well that they did have something there

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.512
in the form of several classified

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.647
documents, boxes of classified documents.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:55.682
And this indictment

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:56.816
overall really lays out

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.617
the narrative

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.619
of what investigators have found

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:00.453
as they've looked

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:01.321
deeper and deeper

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.989
into former President Trump's

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.357
handling of classified documents.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.058
And frankly, it's

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.926
a pretty damning indictment.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:07.660
It sure is.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.862
Zach Cohen, appreciate it.

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:09.529
Thank you very much.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:10.497
Let's talk more about this

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:11.498
damning indictment.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:12.365
Joining me now is Dave

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.666
Aronberg, state attorney

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.101
for Palm Beach County, Florida.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.236
And I've got to say,

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.637
and I was just talking about this

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:18.338
with Victor here,

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:20.440
I mean, it is really an easy read.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.574
There's not a lot of legalese

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.542
in this indictment.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.043
And just like the special counsel

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.879
is urging all Americans to read it,

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:26.479
you really should.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.847
There are so many stunning details,

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:28.815
Dave, to you,

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:29.983
because Trump is accused

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:30.984
of so many things,

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:31.651
you know, lying

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.218
and scheming

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.386
to hold on to these documents,

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.787
showing them off

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.122
and even the way

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:38.024
these documents were stored.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.826
What really stunned you?

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.994
What stuck out to the most

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.564
Good to be with you.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.299
I think what surprised me

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.034
was just the level of involvement

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:50.370
that Donald Trump had in all of this.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.704
He can't just blame this

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.906
on the coffee boy.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:53.840
There are 38 counts.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.909
37 apply to Donald Trump.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.343
And the indictment is powerful

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.111
and damning.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.479
It shows that Trump was involved

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.581
in every step of this process.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:04.217
He packed the boxes, he stored the boxes.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.352
He directed the movement of the boxes.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.254
He tried to hide the boxes

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.222
not just from the government,

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.790
but from his own lawyer.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.592
He asked people to lie about it.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.593
He disseminated

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.728
the classified information to others.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.696
You've got violations

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.097
of the Espionage Act,

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.700
the obstruction laws and lying.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.202
It's really bad for Donald Trump.

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.970
And there was a lot of evidence, right?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:24.604
I mean,

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.239
especially Trump's

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.473
attorney, Evan Corcoran,

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:28.107
his voice

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.676
memos and, of course, some audio

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.644
recordings of Trump himself.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:32.845
In conversations.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:33.880
Tell us about that

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.648
and how critical these this evidence was.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:37.717
It is

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.452
unusual that the key evidence against

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.254
it comes from your own lawyer.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.188
So you bring up a good point

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:42.989
about Evan Corcoran.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:43.957
Usually attorney client

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:45.992
privilege is sacrosanct.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.126
But, you know, Trump has said

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.161
that he wants his lawyers

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.262
to be like Roy Cohn,

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:52.098
the notoriously corrupt lawyer

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.133
friends with Richard Nixon.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:54.734
You know,

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:55.702
as such,

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.570
Trump is free in his mind

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.472
to make these damaging comments

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.840
to his own lawyers,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.609
whether it's Evan Corcoran

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:03.843
or Michael Cohen.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:04.978
And you see

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.279
in the pages of the indictment

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.147
that a lot of this evidence comes

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.816
from Evan Corcoran.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.251
So when the Department of Justice

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.086
got access to Corcoran's

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.921
personal notes, his voice notes,

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:17.490
and these were copious notes, these were

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.858
meticulous notes

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:21.261
under the legal theory of CIA

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:22.795
because that's what Corcoran is doing.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.430
He wanted to cover himself up here

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.331
in case he was ever

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.233
charged with obstruction.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.568
But these notes have come back

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.769
to haunt him.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.604
It's a treasure trove of information

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:32.672
that details

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.473
Trump's involvement

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:34.774
from beginning to end.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:35.275
Of all, it's

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.242
my favorite part

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.111
was the part where Donald Trump

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:40.580
wanted Corcoran to be like Hillary

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.148
Clinton's lawyer, who he believed

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.016
covered up for her,

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.484
deleted all the emails.

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:45.818
This was why he ran for president.

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.587
He said, I'm going to lock you up, right?

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.554
You'd be in jail.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:49.822
Now, he wants his own lawyer

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.658
to be like the lawyer

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:52.825
who guided Hillary Clinton.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:53.760
It's really ironic.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:54.961
And I guess, you know,

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.595
no surprise

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:57.497
when it comes to the high turnover

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:58.965
rate of his legal team. Right.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:04:59.866
So we saw this

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.067
sort of move happen on Friday

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.268
where Trump said

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:02.835
that he was removing

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.637
two of his top attorneys, Jim Trustee

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.572
and John Rowley from the case.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:09.208
And he said that Todd Blanch,

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.577
a defense lawyer, that he hired in April

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.179
after being indicted in Manhattan,

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.747
he will now take the lead.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:15.148
And, of course,

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.582
you had a trustee in Raleigh

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.583
saying that they were resigning

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.852
from the legal team entirely

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.754
What's the strategy here?

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:24.457
The strategy

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:24.991
just to find

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:25.491
a lawyer

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.393
who will take the case in Florida,

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.362
who has knowledge in this area.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:29.796
The problem

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:32.198
is, as is respected as his new lawyer

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.833
is, apparently is not an expert

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.435
in the field of national security.

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:37.437
We lawyers are specialists.

00:05:37.437 --> 00:05:39.105
And you want someone who is used

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:39.639
to this stuff

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.708
dealing with classified information

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.476
because you're going against, gee, Brett

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.677
who's the head of the Department

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:45.678
of Justice's

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.413
Counterintelligence Division,

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.115
and you're going against Jack Smith,

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.350
who's a bulldog.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.551
You want to bring your A-game

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:52.251
and you don't want to bring

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.053
someone who's new to this area.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.054
But this is what happens

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:55.988
with Donald Trump.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.690
You know,
lawyers are reluctant to work for him

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.225
because look at Chris Chi's

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.960
well-respected former solicitor

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:01.961
general, Florida

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:03.363
brought on to help Trump

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.431
given a $3 million retainer.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.899
Trump didn't like his advice.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.701
Guys wanted Trump to be cooperative

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.736
with the DOJ.

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:10.670
Trump rejected it.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.071
He sidelined him.

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:12.872
And now he's stuck

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.040
with whatever he can get.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:14.874
Also, it doesn't help

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:15.708
that Trump continues

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:17.877
to make a tax on prosecutors,

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.512
and he probably will attack

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:20.880
judges, too, in the future.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.814
Not helpful

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.049
if you're representing him

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.518
when you have a former President Trump

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:27.987
attacking this independent

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:29.722
special counsel

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.391
Jack Smith, calling him

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.593
a lunatic and a Trump hater.

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:35.428
Do you see this backfiring in any way

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:38.898
Yeah, I could see that the

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.433
judge is part of Trump's

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:42.435
pretrial release will impose

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:45.204
some restrictions on what Trump can say.

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:46.706
And that's going to be hard

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:47.340
for Donald Trump.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:47.673
He's out there

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:48.307
on the campaign

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:51.577
trail and grievance is his rocket fuel.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.446
I mean, that's what Powers MAGA.

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:55.982
And for him to not be able to attack

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.951
those who he thinks are persecuting him,

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.553
that's going to be hard for him to do.

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.221
And that could be the easiest way

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:04.190
for him to end up in an orange jumpsuit

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.058
by violating a court order.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.026
And lastly,

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:08.361
so the arraignment on Tuesday,

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:09.962
a few days from now, 3 p.m.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:13.366
in Miami, where Trump will be

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:15.201
told about the charges against him,

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:16.469
he will enter a plea.

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:17.170
What are you hearing?

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.105
Because you're there in Palm Beach,

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:20.640
not far from Miami,

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.175
in terms of law enforcement.

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:23.276
Are they scrambling?

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:24.977
We know the DOJ is sending some resources

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:26.012
down there as well.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:27.480
But what is all that going to look like,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.815
how it's going to play out from

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:30.183
a security standpoint?

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.186
Oh, yeah.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:34.320
They're going to be ready this time

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.288
because when Trump is out there

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:36.722
on social media saying,

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:37.222
you know,

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:38.191
get ready for Tuesday,

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:39.325
reminds you of what he said

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:41.260
in advance of January six.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.361
So they're going to be ready.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.529
And a big reason

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.097
that they're going down to Miami,

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:46.999
which really doesn't have a connection

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.234
to this case.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:49.235
This all happened here in Palm

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:51.737
Beach County, Miami is 71 miles away

00:07:52.071 --> 00:07:53.673
But they've got this big courthouse

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:54.941
with a lot of security,

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:56.375
a lot of resources.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:57.376
And I think that's why

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:58.711
they're having it down there.

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.446
They're better equipped, apparently,

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:02.415
to deal with this show

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:04.550
than the smaller courthouses of West Palm

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:05.585
Beach or Fort Pierce.

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:07.587
So I think they will be prepared.

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:08.821
So from a practical standpoint,

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:09.522
it makes sense.

00:08:09.522 --> 00:08:11.390
Dave Aronberg, appreciate you as always.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.458
Thank you very much.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:13.593
Let's talk more about security

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.795
now and go live to Randi Kaye in Miami

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:17.296
outside the federal courthouse.

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:19.298
So on the question of security,

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:21.267
what do we know about logistics so far?

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:25.438
Good morning, Victor.

00:08:25.438 --> 00:08:26.639
What we know is that securing

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:26.973
the scene

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:27.907
really will start

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:30.142
as soon as the former president leaves

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.277
Mar a Lago

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:31.711
to make that

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:33.279
71 mile trip down here

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:34.947
to the federal courthouse in Miami.

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:35.982
I've spoken with some of my law

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:36.849
enforcement contacts,

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:37.650
and they tell me

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:38.784
that we can likely expect

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:39.685
they will

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:41.521
have some sort of exclusive lane

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:43.422
exclusive access on that Interstate

00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:45.458
95 as the former president

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.260
makes his way down here.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.494
They will limit

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:49.862
some of those lanes, perhaps

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:52.698
putting in some lane closures

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:54.901
on that highway also as far as court.

00:08:55.268 --> 00:08:56.936
There will be some type of perimeter

00:08:56.936 --> 00:08:57.370
set up.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.704
They'll look to be keeping

00:08:58.704 --> 00:09:00.206
not only protesters back,

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:02.308
but his supporters back as well.

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:03.242
And this really will be

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:04.176
a coordinated effort

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:05.378
between Secret Service,

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:06.312
the Miami police,

00:09:06.312 --> 00:09:07.647
who will be in charge of detours

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:09.248
and any road closures in the area.

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:11.284
But also the FBI and U.S.

00:09:11.284 --> 00:09:12.685
Marshals as well.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:14.620
They did do a threat assessment here

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.122
at the Miami federal courthouse.

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:17.790
They didn't find any credible threats.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:20.159
They're also monitoring social media

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:21.360
from what I'm told.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.963
Looking for any actionable intelligence.

00:09:23.963 --> 00:09:24.630
They're also looking

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.465
for any calls to action

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:27.934
because they certainly don't want

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:30.036
another January six situation here.

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:32.238
At the Miami federal courthouse.

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:33.573
So they are expecting

00:09:33.573 --> 00:09:35.074
large crowds here, supporters,

00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:36.976
protesters, media, etc.

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:39.145
There will be eyes everywhere

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:40.046
from law enforcement

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:41.581
and one other note, Victor, is

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.683
that this is a very large complex.

00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:44.650
They are certainly going to be

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.352
looking to limit

00:09:46.352 --> 00:09:47.720
Donald Trump's exposure

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.121
to those on the outside.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:50.256
There's a lot of entrances,

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:51.090
a lot of doors here.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:51.691
Very likely

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:52.291
they will take him

00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:53.793
in one of the back doors

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:54.360
where most people

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.695
won't be able to see him,

00:09:55.695 --> 00:09:57.263
probably bring him through the basement

00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:58.230
of this courthouse,

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.799
up to the courtroom for his arraignment.

00:09:59.799 --> 00:10:00.533
Victor,

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.601
you have been speaking

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:04.170
with some of the Trump supporters there.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.071
What have you been hearing

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:08.574
Yeah, we spent

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:09.542
the last couple of days at Mar

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:11.611
a Lago talking to some of his supporters.

00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:13.346
And, you know, they

00:10:13.346 --> 00:10:15.414
they just do not believe

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:17.283
that the former president

00:10:17.283 --> 00:10:18.751
had any classified documents.

00:10:18.751 --> 00:10:19.518
In fact,
I told them

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:21.854
what was in the indictment yesterday

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:22.488
and I showed them

00:10:22.488 --> 00:10:23.155
the pictures

00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:23.889
of these

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:26.058
boxes of alleged documents in the shower

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:27.693
in the bathroom, in the ballroom.

00:10:27.693 --> 00:10:28.694
And they said

00:10:28.694 --> 00:10:30.363
that those pictures were doctored

00:10:30.363 --> 00:10:31.564
or they were fake.

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:33.165
They believe if he did have any documents

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:34.367
there, they were planted.

00:10:34.367 --> 00:10:35.668
And they just don't believe

00:10:35.668 --> 00:10:36.168
that he would do

00:10:36.168 --> 00:10:37.703
anything like this Victor.

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:39.238
All right. Randi Kaye, thank you.

